el"],["Republican","Sherveal Mimes"],["Republican","Lola Waterman"],["Conservative","Betsey Jean Jacques"],["Conservative","William D. Spain Jr"],["Conservative","Sherveal Mimes"],["Conservative","Lola Waterman"]]},"QUEENS":{"t":"Justice of the Supreme Court, 11th Judicial District, Queens County","o":"Justice of the Supreme Court","d":"11th Judicial District, Queens County","vf":3,"c":[["Edwin I. Novillo",["Democratic"],null],["Oma D. Phillips",["Democratic"],null],["Gail A. Adams",["Democratic"],null],["David A. Bellon",["Republican"],null],["Gary Muraca",["Republican"],null]],"lines":[["Democratic","Edwin I. Novillo"],["Democratic","Oma D. Phillips"],["Democratic","Gail A. Adams"],["Republican","David A. Bellon"],["Republican","Gary Muraca"]]},"BRONX":{"t":"Justice of the Supreme Court, 12th Judicial District, Bronx County","o":"Justice of the Supreme Court","d":"12th Judicial District, Bronx County","vf":1,"c":[["Alvin M. Yearwood",["Democratic"],null]],"lines":[["Democratic","Alvin M. Yearwood"]]},"STATEN ISLAND":{"t":"Justice of the Supreme Court, 13th Judicial District, Richmond County","o":"Justice of the Supreme Court","d":"13th Judicial District, Richmond County","vf":1,"c":[["Kelvin Richards",["Democratic"],null],["Michael J. Pinto",["Republican"],null]],"lines":[["Democratic","Kelvin Richards"],["Republican","Michael J. Pinto"]]}},"questions":[{"n":1,"t":"Speed Up Process for Granting a Revocable Consent to Use Public Space","s":"Simplify process to use public space for uses such as ramps, planters and cafes, by removing mandatory hearings and Council disapproval of sidewalk cafes, while maintaining community and Council input."},{"n":2,"t":"Reduce City Contractor Paperwork; Require Regular Meetings of Procurement Policy Board","s":"Reduce paperwork for City contractors by authorizing Procurement Policy Board to simplify contractor questionnaire. Require quarterly meetings of the Procurement Policy Board. Remove mandatory hearing for required client services report."},{"n":3,"t":"Speed Up Street Safety Projects, Disposition of Unused City Property, Office Leasing","s":"Simplify review of street safety projects to reduce construction timelines. Fast track disposition of unused City property with approval from City Planning Commission. Expedite leasing offices used for City workforce."},{"n":4,"t":"Simplify Building Permitting and Move Waterfront Permitting to Department of Buildings","s":"Create centralized construction permits hub to simplify permitting. Move waterfront permitting from Department of Small Business Services to Department of Buildings. Allow construction approval by additional Department of Buildings officials."},{"n":5,"t":"Set Contribution Targets for Rainy Day Fund to Promote Sufficient Budgetary Reserves","s":"Set target amount of money to hold in reserve funds, including rainy day fund, to address unexpected financial hardships in future years, and require development of methodology to calculate contributions."}],"qsrc":"Commission on Government Efficiency, the 2026 New York City Charter Revision Commission. Appendix A, Proposed Questions, adopted at the final public meeting on July 23, 2026."}